Description: Allocate the S3M pattern pointer array with the pointer size
 The S3M loader allocated 4 bytes per pattern pointer. On 64-bit
 architectures the array overflowed and corrupted the heap, so loading any
 S3M module aborted with a glibc malloc assertion.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-12
--- a/loads3m.c
+++ b/loads3m.c
@@ -672,7 +672,7 @@
     CHECKHEAP
 
     /* Allocate memory for pattern pointers: */
-    if ( (error = memAlloc(4 * module->numPatts,
+    if ( (error = memAlloc(sizeof(gmpPattern*) * module->numPatts,
         (void**) &module->patterns)) != OK )
         PASSERR()
 
